\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A sphere-packing configuration is a collection of centers with prescribed minimum pairwise separation. A periodic configuration repeats under a lattice of translations. Projection changes candidate coordinates to satisfy the chosen geometric constraints.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The training distribution, projection, extrapolation guarantee, and downstream-improvement criterion are not specified.

Source-record limitation: Generative-model extrapolation and downstream improvement are requested without a distribution or guarantee.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can one conditional generative model trained across different numbers of balls and dimensions extrapolate to larger sphere-packing instances while preserving or improving minimum separation after projection? Extend projection-corrected flow-matching methods from finite boxes to periodic packings and establish when the resulting candidates improve downstream optimization. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2025/43}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-22.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Extend generated packing configurations across sizes, dimensions, and periodic geometries.

